Wed Oct 14 06:54:38 UTC 2026
$PROBLEM    single_iv_cov_s: one-population twin of mixture_iv_cov
;           (#1956),S matrix
; CL = TVCL*EXP(ETA), V = TVV on mixture_iv.csv, at the one-population MLE found by

; tests/nonmem/mixture_iv_cov_score_oracle.py --single (6 sig. fig.), MAXEVAL=0.

; Shows whether NONMEM's S differs from ferx's on a model with no $MIX at all.
$INPUT      ID TIME DV AMT EVID CMT WT
$DATA      mixture_iv.csv IGNORE=@
$SUBROUTINE ADVAN1 TRANS2
$PK
  CL = THETA(1) * EXP(ETA(1))
  V  = THETA(2)
  S1 = V

$ERROR
  IPRED = F
  Y = IPRED * (1.0 + EPS(1))

$THETA  (0.01,1.76783,100.0) ; TVCL
 (0.1,9.77524,1000.0) ; V
$OMEGA  0.09  FIX
$SIGMA  0.04  FIX
$ESTIMATION METHOD=1 INTER MAXEVAL=0 NOABORT
$COVARIANCE MATRIX=S PRINT=E


NM-TRAN MESSAGES
  
 WARNINGS AND ERRORS (IF ANY) FOR PROBLEM    1
             
 (WARNING  2) NM-TRAN INFERS THAT THE DATA ARE POPULATION.
             
 (WARNING  111) $COVARIANCE: IN THE ABSENCE OF $ESTIM OR $MSFI, OR WITH
 $ESTIM MAXEVAL=0, THE UNCONDITIONAL OPTION IS REQUIRED. NM-TRAN HAS
 SUPPLIED THIS OPTION.
  
Note: Analytical 2nd Derivatives are constructed in FSUBS but are never used.
      You may insert $ABBR DERIV2=NO after the first $PROB to save FSUBS construction and compilation time
  

